# Baseline for dev/check_fork_markers.py — the fork-content audit.
#
# Format: `path/glob  # reason`. Every entry MUST carry a reason; the script
# refuses to run otherwise. This list is a ROLLOUT SCHEDULE, not a set of
# permanent exemptions: each entry means "the fork hunks in this file are not yet
# annotated", and the list is meant to shrink. Removing an entry is the definition
# of done for bringing a file under the convention.
#
# A file leaves this list one of two ways:
#
#   1. CONVERGE — make it byte-identical to upstream/main, retiring it as a
#      drop site forever. Only when our delta is genuinely not worth carrying.
#   2. MARK — put a `# Fork:` comment inside every diverging top-level
#      definition saying what deviates and why, or a fork boundary banner if the
#      fork content is a contiguous tail block.
#
# THE TRAP, and it is the whole reason this file has reasons rather than just
# paths: a site that differs from upstream is NOT automatically fork work. It can
# equally be content a merge resolution DROPPED, in which case marking it
# `# Fork:` launders a bug into a documented feature and no later audit will ever
# question it again. Establish provenance first (`git log -S`, `git merge-base
# --is-ancestor` against BOTH HEAD and upstream/main) exactly as AGENTS.md
# requires. Entries below tagged LEADS have known dropped-hunk candidates from
# `dev/find_dropped_hunks.py`; resolve those before marking anything in the file.
#
# Worked example of the trap, found while building this check:
# speculative/drafters/gemma4_assistant/masks.py was documented in AGENTS.md as a
# "deliberate divergence — must keep its absolute import". It was not. Upstream's
# a492e47d (#1494) changed masks.py to a relative import AND rewrote its test's
# module fakes to match; only the first half was dropped here, so our test still
# faked `mlx_lm.models.cache` (inert — the real mlx_vlm module loads anyway) and
# the absolute import was a workaround for the missing half. Taking BOTH halves
# made both files byte-identical to upstream with the test still passing. Marking
# masks.py `# Fork:` would have frozen that mistake permanently.
#
# RESOLVED 2026-08-09 (second pass), removed from this list:
#   models/qwen3_5_moe/qwen3_5_moe.py  — restored #1450's `mid` slicing (our copy had
#     #722's pre-fix `mx.split`); the unfused branch is fork work (f0d50c90, landed in
#     parallel with upstream's #1472) and now carries a `# Fork:` marker.
#   trainer/utils.py + tests/test_trainer_utils.py — both now BYTE-IDENTICAL to
#     upstream. 13d1ff4e unified the text-model LoRA path; our copy kept a separate
#     `adapter_utils.load_adapters` branch whose config handling was strictly weaker
#     (AttributeError on a missing `num_layers`, no `keys` targeting, legacy configs
#     skipped). Same-named test on each side, adapted to each implementation.
#   tests/test_utils.py — union-merged with upstream. Zero fork-only *definitions* but
#     real fork content in *bodies*, so not a clean checkout. Its 5 "pre-existing
#     failures" were stale test code; now 34 passed / 0 failed AND re-enabled in the
#     suite (the --ignore is gone).
#
#   tests/test_batch_quantized_cache.py — union-merged with upstream (fourth pass).
#     17 fork-only definitions, 12 upstream-only, and the one shared class differed
#     only by a method we lacked. Fork content is now two classes below a boundary
#     banner plus three marked imports; 12 .symbol-exclusions entries retired.
#
#   tests/test_speculative.py — union-merged (fourth pass). Only TWO fork-only
#     definitions in 3371 lines; the single shared test that differed did so by
#     4b15cc5's deliberate one-ULP bound, now marked. 11 .symbol-exclusions retired.
#
# Current standing (2026-08-09): 19 files, down from 32. Every
